istribution there could be  other  properties that we want good properties  that we want the hypothesis  to have with respect to the unknown  distribution for instance nobody wants a  hypothesis to  you know be algorithmically fair in some  sense or we want it to be  safe you know it's a self-driving car  and we wanted  some some guarantees that it uh  um it's safe so those are different  kinds of properties that the hypothesis  can have with respect to the unknown  distribution  and one could imagine developing uh  verification  interactive proofs for those properties  and not for the accuracy  or in addition to the accuracy um  okay so that pretty much wraps up uh  my talk um thank you very much for  watching and we'll be um  hanging out on the slack channel and  we'll be very happy to  to answer any questions you might have  thank you
 

